title start
kind: research
tags: research notes
Research page: does plain text make notes easier to find
title end

paragraph start
Use a research page when you investigate one question and want a reader to find the method and the results at once.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Abstract
title end

paragraph start
We ask whether plain text files help a person find an old note faster than a note app does. Twenty notes were searched by hand and by grep on one machine. Grep found every note and the app missed some. The test was small and used one person.
answer start
for: qfdb2b2
asked: Does it state the question, the method, the result and a limit?
Yes. It names the question, the method, the result and one limit.
answer end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Introduction
title end

paragraph start
People keep notes for years and then cannot find them. If the storage format decides how fast a note is found, choosing it well saves time every day.
answer start
for: q075df6
asked: Does it say why the question matters?
Yes. The cost is paid every day, for years.
answer end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Methods
title end

paragraph start
The same twenty notes were stored twice, as text files and in an app. For each note a search phrase was written first, then both stores were searched with it.
answer start
for: q6b4b50
asked: Could a reader repeat this from the text alone?
Yes, with the phrase list and the command below.
answer end
paragraph end

code start
language: bash
grep -rl meeting notes/
code end

comment start
A command goes in a code block so a reader can copy it. Always write the language under the start line.
comment end
section end

section start
title start
Results
title end

paragraph start
Grep returned all twenty notes. The app returned seventeen and ranked four of them below the first page.
answer start
for: q1e9f6a
asked: Does every claim point to evidence?
Yes. Each count comes from the search log.
answer end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Discussion
title end

paragraph start
Plain text looks better for finding notes, but one person and twenty notes show little. A larger test with several people is needed.
answer start
for: qabfedd
asked: What do these results not show?
They do not show how it scales, or whether other people would find the same.
answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: find three people to repeat the test
A repeat with other people would settle the limit above.
paragraph end
